WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.689 --> 00:00:06.090
In the lead-up to the 2020 Academy Awards,
set to air on Sunday, February 9, Adam Sandler

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.140
was near the head of the pack for Best Actor
contenders.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.440
For his performance as Diamond District jeweler
and self-destructive gambling addict Howard

00:00:13.449 --> 00:00:18.700
Ratner in the Safdie brothers' crime thriller
Uncut Gems, Sandler had most everyone believing

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.440
he'd land at least a nomination for the coveted
award.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.560
"That's the dumbest f---ing bet I ever heard."

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.360
However, when the list of 2020 Oscar nominations
rolled out, Sandler's name was nowhere to

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.730
be found, despite the fact that viewers everywhere
thought he'd be a shoo-in.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.820
Now, The New York Post has run quotes from
an anonymous Academy member who commented

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:41.550
on some of the actors who didn't score Oscar
nominations this year: Dolemite Is My Name

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:46.059
star Eddie Murphy, Hustlers lead Jennifer
Lopez, The Farewell actress Awkwafina, and,

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:47.059
of course, Sandler.

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:53.179
The nameless actor revealed the real reason
why Adam Sandler was snubbed, and the answer

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:53.980
isn't pretty.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.520
Let's not forget: Adam Sandler is a seriously
funny actor.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.120
"Stay here.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.540
Stay as long as you can.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.180
For the love of God, cherish it!"

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:12.460
He's split sides in films like Happy Gilmore,
Billy Madison, The Waterboy, The Wedding Singer,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.960
Big Daddy, and more, gaining fame as much
more than a former Saturday Night Live player.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.760
In the 2000s, Sandler ventured into more dramatic
territory with Spanglish, Punch-Drunk Love,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.200
and Funny People, effectively proving he wasn't
a one-trick pony.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.060
But at a certain point, Sandler's track record
grew spotty when he began signing on to films

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.800
that were, well…less-than-spectacular.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:39.780
He racked up Razzies, basically the ugly step-sister
to the merit-based award ceremonies, for Just

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:45.390
Go With It and Jack and Jill, two of Sandler's
worst movies ever, and tarnished his reputation

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.260
in the process.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:50.780
It's only been in recent years, through his
turns in films like Netflix's The Meyerowitz

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:56.340
Stories and now Uncut Gems, that Sandler has
begun to shed his "King of Bad Movies" moniker.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.620
Sadly, Oscars voters have a stronger memory
than the general public does.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.980
The reason why he didn't receive an Oscar
nomination, according to the well-known character

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:10.429
actor and member of the Academy, is because
people don't associate the name "Adam Sandler"

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.770
with accolades as prestigious as Academy Awards.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:14.770
The source claimed:

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.920
"There are a lot of movies, a lot of performances
per year for us to watch.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.900
Unfortunately, actors become brands.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.840
Sandler's brand doesn't scream 'Oscar.'"

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:24.660
Ouch.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.080
During an appearance on The Howard Stern Show
in early December 2019, Sandler threatened

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.650
revenge on the movie-going masses if he didn't
nab an Academy Award for his performance in

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:34.520
Uncut Gems.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.240
The actor warned that he would take a role
in an unbelievably bad movie to make everyone

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.040
regret not nominating him for, and, more importantly,
awarding him with, an Oscar.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.020
Sandler said:

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:50.740
"If I don't get it, I'm going to f---ing come
back and do one again that is so bad on purpose

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.080
just to make you all pay.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.340
That's how I get them."

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.470
He added that though it would be a, quote,
"funny big thing" for him to receive an Oscar

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.410
nomination, he would be "there to win" if
it actually happened.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:07.080
We all know that it didn't, and it seems Sandler's
plan for payback could still be intact.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.600
Given that his filmography isn't exactly packed
wall to wall with winners, the actor doesn't

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.230
have much to lose if he does go through with
making a terrible film, except the respect

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.620
of the Academy voting body.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.099
In response to Sandler's comments on The Howard
Stern Show, one member allegedly complained

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:26.670
that the actor has an "arrogance" to him,
and that his threat showed, quote, "a lack

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.340
of respect."

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.920
For everyone's sake, hopefully Sandler sticks
to more substantial gigs and doesn't actually

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.360
make a total stinker to follow up Uncut Gems.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.200
He may not have been placed in the running
for Oscars gold following his turn in the

00:03:38.209 --> 00:03:43.210
film, but the fact that he generated genuine
buzz for a Best Actor award speaks volumes.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:48.060
May Sandler's future, and ours, feature more
roles like Howard Ratner and fewer like…well…

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.440
"I feel like Julia Roberts in that movie!"

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.440
"Pretty Woman?"

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.220
"No, the one where she's a hooker!"

